                    <h3 class="font-bold text-[13px] tracking-widest">METHODOLOGY & SOURCES</h3>
                    <p class="text-[13px] text-slate-500 leading-6 mt-2">We reviewed 23 no credit check banks using CFPB complaint database, FDIC BankFind, and bureau disclosure docs. We prioritize: (1) No ChexSystems/credit pull for checking, (2) Reports to all 3 bureaus (Experian, Equifax, TransUnion), (3) Fees <$10 /mo, (4) US-based support. Data as of Oct 2026. Sources: <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/" class="underline">CFPB</a>, <a href="https://www.experian.com/" class="underline">Experian</a>, <a href="https://www.equifax.com/" class="underline">Equifax</a>. We did not accept payment for placement.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="prose mt-10">
                    <h2>What is a no credit check bank account?</h2>
                    <p>A no credit check bank account means the bank does <b>not</b> use your FICO or credit history to approve you. Most fintechs in this guide also skip ChexSystems, which means even if you've had overdrafts or a closed account before, you can still get approved. According to the <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-a-second-chance-bank-account-en-2113/" class="underline">CFPB</a>, second-chance accounts are designed for consumers denied by traditional banks.</p>
                    <p>But opening the account alone does <b>NOT</b> build credit. Checking accounts in the US do not report to credit bureaus unless they include a credit-building feature — like Chime Credit Builder secured Visa or Self's Credit Builder loan linked to savings.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><b>No credit check to open:</b> You need only ID, US address, and usually SSN or ITIN. Some allow ITIN only.</li>
                        <li><b>Credit building:</b> Only happens if on-time payments are reported to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion.</li>
                        <li><b>No SSN options:</b> We flag which ones accept ITIN instead of SSN below — critical for newcomers and undocumented consumers.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>Comparison: Best No Credit Check Banks That Build Credit (2026)</h2>
                    <p>We compared the top 5 for fees, reporting, and ChexSystems policy for US consumers.</p>
