                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
                    <h3>Can a bank account build credit with no credit check?</h3>
                    <p>Yes, but only if the bank offers a credit-building add-on that reports to bureaus. Regular checking never builds credit. Chime Credit Builder, Self Builder, Current Build, and Varo Believe report to all 3 without credit check for the builder product.</p>

                    <h3>Which no credit check bank reports to all 3 bureaus?</h3>
                    <p>Chime, Self, Current Build, and Varo Believe report to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion. MoneyLion reports to at least 2, sometimes all 3 depending on plan. Verify in app settings under credit reporting consent.</p>

                    <h3>Can I open a bank account online with no SSN in the US?</h3>
                    <p>Some fintechs like Current allow ITIN to open checking. However, to build credit and have it report to bureaus to generate a FICO, you still need an SSN. ITIN-only file may not score at Experian until SSN is added. No bank can report without some tax ID.</p>

                    <h3>Are no credit check banks safe? Are they FDIC insured?</h3>
                    <p>Varo is a chartered bank FDIC insured $250k. Chime, Current, Self, MoneyLion are fintechs where banking services are provided by partner banks (Bancorp, etc.) and funds may be FDIC insured via partner — check fine print. All use encryption, but they are not credit bureaus themselves.</p>

                    <h3>What is the best account if I was denied due to ChexSystems?</h3>
                    <p>All 5 on this list do not use ChexSystems to deny checking: Chime, Current, Varo, Self wallet, MoneyLion RoarMoney. If you failed ChexSystems at Chase/Wells, start with Chime or Current — approval 99%+ with valid US ID per internal data.</p>
                </div>

